ANR frame generation (Neural Rendering)

The per-app frame generation switch (rust/core/session/src/neural.rs, rust/host/stream/src/neural.rs)
installs ANR frame generation by apex-compute (https://github.com/apex-compute/ANR),
release FG-V.B16, into a game's folder. Its authors publish no license for it.
Rubylight does not host, bundle, mirror or modify any of its files: at the user's
request the host downloads the release's anr-fg-V.B16-full.zip and
anr-fg-V.B16-addon.zip from that GitHub release on the user's PC, checks them against
the SHA-256 Rubylight pins, GitHub's digests and the release's SHA256SUMS.txt, and
copies the files unmodified. The full package carries OptiScaler (GPL-3.0) with its
license texts, which are copied with it. The console and Nightjar call the feature
frame generation and do not brand it with the mod's name.

AMDNR (Rubylight 3.0's Neural Rendering)

Rubylight 3.0's per-app Neural Rendering switch installed AMDNR by 3zwr1
(https://github.com/3zwr1/AMD-NR---OptiScaler), a GPL-3.0 licensed fork of
